From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: use rdcycle for the golden counter

Root cause: the fixture rejects every RISC-V build after providing only an
x86 `rdtsc` implementation. Use the architectural RISC-V cycle CSR through a
minimal inline-assembly branch. This patch is downstream-only and is removed
when fixture version 1.0 is retired.

Patch-Source: repository golden acceptance fixture
Patch-License: MIT
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (test fixture; automated upstream writes forbidden)
---
 golden_inline.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/golden_inline.c b/golden_inline.c
index 6318021..71468e7 100644
--- a/golden_inline.c
+++ b/golden_inline.c
@@ -9,7 +9,9 @@ static unsigned long read_counter(void)
     __asm__ volatile("rdtsc" : "=a"(low), "=d"(high));
     return ((unsigned long)high << 32) | low;
 #elif defined(__riscv)
-#error "golden failure: x86-only counter lacks a RISC-V implementation"
+    unsigned long value;
+    __asm__ volatile("rdcycle %0" : "=r"(value));
+    return value;
 #else
     return 0;
 #endif
